```sql
CREATE TABLE moves(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, tick INTEGER, amount INTEGER);
INSERT INTO moves VALUES (1,1,4),(2,1,7),(3,2,3);
SELECT id, SUM(amount) OVER (ORDER BY tick RANGE BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW) AS peers_total, SUM(amount) OVER (ORDER BY tick,id ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW) AS row_total
FROM moves
ORDER BY id;
```
SUM(amount) adds the amounts in each frame. UNBOUNDED PRECEDING starts at the partition beginning. The RANGE order is tick alone, so both tick 1 rows share total 11. The ROWS order tick,id is unique, giving 4 then 11 then 14. Adding id to RANGE would remove those peer ties; it would answer a different ordering question.

