```sql
CREATE TABLE sessions(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, team TEXT, done INTEGER, minutes INTEGER);
INSERT INTO sessions VALUES (1,'fern',1,10),(2,'fern',0,20),(3,'moss',0,7);
SELECT team, COUNT(*) AS all_rows, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE done=1) AS done_rows, SUM(minutes) FILTER (WHERE done=1) AS done_minutes
FROM sessions
GROUP BY team
ORDER BY team;
```
COUNT(*) counts input rows, so the filtered count for moss is 0. SUM(minutes) adds non-NULL minute values; with no matching inputs it returns NULL, not 0. Fern has 2 total rows but only 1 completed row and 10 completed minutes. FILTER is a clause, not a function call.

