```sql
PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON;
CREATE TABLE folders(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY);
CREATE TABLE notes(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, folder_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES folders(id) ON DELETE CASCADE);
INSERT INTO folders VALUES (1),(2);
INSERT INTO notes VALUES (10,1),(11,1),(12,2);
DELETE
FROM folders
WHERE id=1;
SELECT id,folder_id
FROM notes
ORDER BY id;
```
Only note 12 in folder 2 remains. PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON must run before opening a transaction; changing it inside a transaction does not enable enforcement. The child REFERENCES clause names folders(id), and ON DELETE CASCADE states the deletion action. No unrelated folder or note is removed.

